/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - Strength: σmax ≤ σallow = Syt/n; stiffness: δmax ≤ δallow, θ ≤ θallow
   - σmax is the largest working stress (MPa) and n the factor of safety; δmax is the largest deflection (mm) and θ the angle of twist (rad or degrees); the limits come from the function of the machine or from a design guide.
   - Bending strength depends on the section modulus Z = I/c, bending stiffness on the second moment I.
   - δ = PL/(AE); θ = TL/(GJ)
   - δ is the extension of a bar of length L (mm) and area A (mm²) under an axial load P (N); θ is the angle of twist (rad) of a shaft of length L under torque T (N·mm); E and G are the moduli of elasticity and rigidity (N/mm²); J is the polar s
   - In the table, P is a point load (N), w a load per unit length (N/mm), L the span (mm), E the modulus of elasticity (N/mm²) and I the second moment of area of the section about the bending axis (mm⁴).
   - Figure 1.8.1 plots both requirements for the beam of the first worked example.
*/
