/* book Worked example 2: Q: A solid steel shaft transmits 10 kW at 240 rpm. The allowable shear stress is 40 MPa, the twist must not exceed 0.25° per metre, and G = 80 GPa. Find the diameter.
   1. Torque: T = 60 × 10,000/(2π × 240) = 397.9 N·m = 397,887 N·mm.
   2. Strength: 16T/(πd³) ≤ 40, so d³ ≥ 16 × 397,887/(π × 40) = 50,661 and d ≥ 37.0 mm.
   3. Stiffness: θ = 0.25° = 0.25 × π/180 = 4.363 × 10⁻³ rad over L = 1000 mm. θ = TL/(GJ) = 32TL/(πGd⁴), so d⁴ ≥ 32 × 397,887 × 1000/(π × 80,000 × 4.363 × 10⁻³) = 1.161 × 10⁷ and d ≥ 58.4 mm.
   4. Stiffness governs. Take the standard size d = 60 mm.
   5. Recheck: J = π × 60⁴/32 = 1.272 × 10⁶ mm⁴; θ = 397,887 × 1000/(80,000 × 1.272 × 10⁶) = 3.91 × 10⁻³ rad = 0.224° per metre; τ = 16 × 397,887/(π × 60³) = 9.38 MPa.
   Answer: Stiffness governs: d ≥ 58.4 mm against 37.0 mm for strength. Use 60 mm; the twist is 0.224°/m and the shear stress only 9.4 MPa. */
